# `display=text` on the kernel command line keeps the 80x25 VGA text screen,
# whatever graphics card there is: the way back when graphics go wrong.
@args display=text
$ display
driver: text (VGA text mode, no graphics)
text: 80x25 characters
@screenshot 720x400 text
$ display test
display test: needs a graphics mode, and this is the text screen
$ display mode 1280x720
display mode 1280x720: no graphics driver is in use (this is the text screen)
$ help
$ echo the text screen still scrolls
the text screen still scrolls
@screenshot 720x400 text
